  "question": {
    "text": "A frictionless piston-cylinder based enclosure contains some amount of gas at a pressure of $400 \\mathrm{kPa}$. Then heat is transferred fo the gas at constant pressure in a quasi-static process. The piston moves up slowly through a height of $10 \\mathrm{cm} .$ If the piston has a cross-sectional area of $0.3 \\mathrm{m}^{2},$ the work done by the gas in this process is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "HKEwe",
      "text": "$6 \\mathrm{kJ}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "jwfU7",
      "text": "$12 \\mathrm{kJ}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0n33v",
      "text": "$7.5 \\mathrm{kJ}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ftEAf",
      "text": "$24 \\mathrm{kJ}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$W_{\\text {constant pressure }}=p \\times \\Delta V$ $=400 \\times 10^{3} \\times 0.3 \\times 10 \\times 10^{-2}$\r\n$=400 \\times 10 \\times 3$\r\n$=12000=12 \\mathrm{kJ}$",
